From: Sergey <onufriev.serg@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: mediatek: EN7528: size the AHB to PCIe window by log2

The size field of PCIE_AHB_TRANS_BASE0_L on EN7528 is log2 of the window
size: the vendor kernel programs 0x20000015 for a 2 MiB window at
0x20000000. fls() gives one more, so the window becomes twice as large as
the memory resource. For port1 at 0x28000000 with 128 MiB this is a
256 MiB window that is not aligned to its size; the hardware then decodes
it as 0x20000000-0x2fffffff, which also covers port0's memory, and any
memory access to a device behind port0 hangs the bus. With log2 the two
128 MiB windows are aligned and disjoint, and both ports work at the
same time (Nokia G-1426-MA: MT7915 on port1, its second PCIe interface
on port0).

Signed-off-by: Sergey <onufriev.serg@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-mediatek.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-mediatek.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-mediatek.c
@@ -834,7 +834,7 @@ static int mtk_pcie_startup_port_en7528(
 
 	/* Set AHB to PCIe translation windows */
 	val = lower_32_bits(mem->start) |
-	      AHB2PCIE_SIZE(fls(resource_size(mem)));
+	      AHB2PCIE_SIZE(ilog2(resource_size(mem)));
 	writel(val, port->base + PCIE_AHB_TRANS_BASE0_L);
 
 	val = upper_32_bits(mem->start);
